35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that chasing individual payments takes six hours a month, but a yearly collection takes only one.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, that confirms my fear. The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, yet a third of renewals needed chasing. We cannot guess the fee.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, the data confirms my worry. Nine tasters refused a full-year commitment, and eleven mid-year joiners needed manual calculations. The current structure is too rigid for newcomers.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, nine tasters refusing a full year? That’s the hesitation I see. I need a structure that lets people dip a toe in, not commit to a whole year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, eleven manual calculations? That is a disaster. @May, the sign-in sheets show a quarter of us doing two-thirds of the work. The fee is a distraction.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, that is a lot of fixed costs. @Minako, I am sorry the manual work was so hard for you.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, the fixed costs mean we need a buffer. @Shunichi, if the workload is skewed, the fee must reflect that reality, not just the average.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shunichi, the workload is real, but the fee structure is what keeps the door open. If newcomers feel the pressure, they leave.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the workload is real, but the hesitation is killing us. If the fee feels like a trap, people won’t show up.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, hesitation is a symptom. The real issue is that a few people carry the load while others pay the same. I need to see who is actually doing the work.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I hear you. But if the books are too hard, people quit. I want a way that is gentle for everyone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, gentleness is not a financial strategy. We need a baseline that covers the fixed costs without relying on guesswork.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, a baseline is necessary, but it must not be a barrier. If the entry point is too high, we lose the people who keep us alive.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, a baseline is fine, but it cannot be a wall. If the price makes people hesitate, we lose the very people who make this club worth joining.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, a baseline is fine, but it ignores the reality. If the fee doesn't account for who actually shows up, we are just paying for empty chairs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I am still thinking about the hours. Six hours a month is so much time. I want to make sure the next person is not overwhelmed.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will not set a fee on hope. The numbers show a gap. We need a structure that covers the fixed costs without guessing.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I am confident the data supports a flexible entry point. We must protect the anonymity that allows newcomers to drift in without pressure.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I am done hesitating. The data proves the current structure is a trap. I need a way in that doesn't feel like a commitment to a whole year.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I am done guessing. The data is clear: a few people do the work, the rest pay for empty chairs. We need a structure that reflects actual participation, not just headcount.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
