66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, Option A is a single collection. It eliminates the chasing. The bank data proves that spreading payments creates the burden, not the fee itself.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, I agree. Option A is the only one that keeps contributions invisible. It protects the quiet drift that defines us.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, invisibility is just another word for hesitation. If I have to guess what I owe, I won’t show up. Option B lets me pay only when I actually join in.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
